# Supabase TypeScript – update/insert

Vercel `next build` fails when you pass `Record<string, any>` into Supabase `.update()` / `.insert()`.
Supabase then expects `{ [x: string]: never }` / typed Row payload → **TS2345**.

## Never do this

```typescript
const updates: Record<string, any> = {};
await supabase.from('credential_pg').update(updates);
await supabase.from('credential_pg').update(updates as any); // band-aid, avoid
```

## Always do this

```typescript
import type { Database } from '@/lib/database.types';

type CredentialUpdate = Database['public']['Tables']['credential_pg']['Update'];
type CredentialInsert = Database['public']['Tables']['credential_pg']['Insert'];

const updates: CredentialUpdate = { email: 'x@y.cz' };
await supabase.from('credential_pg').update(updates);

const row: CredentialInsert = { email: 'x@y.cz' };
await supabase.from('credential_pg').insert(row);
```

## Dynamic keys

If you build the payload in a loop, keep the **variable typed** as `Update`/`Insert`, and only cast the assignment:

```typescript
const updates: CredentialUpdate = {};
for (const key of allowedKeys) {
  if (key in body) {
    (updates as Record<string, unknown>)[key] = body[key];
  }
}
await supabase.from('credential_pg').update(updates);
```

## Checklist before finishing API work

1. Payload for `.update()` / `.insert()` uses `Database['public']['Tables'][...]['Update'|'Insert']`
2. No `Record<string, any>` passed into Supabase mutations
3. Prefer `npx tsc --noEmit` locally (or `npm run build`) before push — Vercel fails on the same check
